MODIFICATIONS:
- Applied fix from PR #21 (https://github.com/imbus/robotframework-debug/pull/21)
  * Fixed AttributeError in keywords command when KeywordDoc lacks shortdoc attribute
  * Superseded: Robot Framework 7 keyword documentation always has shortdoc
- The code is maintained as part of YARF: it is linted, type-checked and
  fully covered by the YARF test suite
- Only the REPL library mode used by the YARF interactive console is kept:
  the listener, step mode (F7-F10, Shift+Tab), source listing commands,
  standalone shell and Robot Framework 6 compatibility code were removed
- Fixed the library and resource documentation builders for Robot
  Framework 7.5, which broke keyword completion and the keywords command
- Variables assigned inside FOR, IF, WHILE and TRY blocks are reported
- The `style` command reports unknown styles instead of failing
- The prompt-toolkit key bindings moved to keybindings.py, and the command
  loop was merged into ReplCmd in debugcmd.py
- Added type hints and Google style docstrings

REASON FOR VENDORING:
The upstream project is no longer actively maintained, and critical bug fixes
(such as PR #21) are not being merged. This vendored version ensures the
library remains functional for yarf's requirements.

The vendored code includes the following modules from the RobotDebug package:
- cmdcompleter.py (command completion functionality)
- debugcmd.py (REPL commands and keyword execution)
- history_app.py (command history management)
- keybindings.py (prompt key bindings)
- lexer.py (syntax highlighting)
- RobotDebug.py (main debug library interface)
- robotkeyword.py (Robot Framework keyword handling)
- robotlib.py (Robot Framework library utilities)
- styles.py (styling configuration)

All original copyright notices and attribution are preserved.
